  data:  # 43e3
    kind: work_item  # 43e3
    title: "route-marker symbols are kind=function with a source language whatever they stand for (a java handler METHOD, a ts/go registration CALL): ADR-0027 kind and ADR-0031 language/protocol_origin need a ruling on what a route marker represents"  # 43e3
    status: todo_hard  # 43e3
    priority: 3  # 43e3
    parent:  # 43e3
    tags:  # 43e3
    - symbol_kind  # 43e3
    - axis  # 43e3
    - framework  # 43e3
    isbefore: []  # 43e3
    duplicate_of: []  # 43e3
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 43e3
    pr_ref:  # 43e3
    description: "Found 2026-10-27 by WI-ziruv, production `hypergumbo survey` on dev 7207fb0ecf. Needs a ruling before any fix.\n\nRoute-marker symbols (pass route-materializer; framework_patterns.py:151 mints kind=\"function\", \"the ADR-0027 Phase-3 route->function fold\") are kind=function whatever they stand for:\n- java: `@GetMapping(\"/a\") String routed()` inside a @RestController -> a node \"GET /a\", kind=function, language=java, meta.materialized_from=...:Ctl.routed:method. The handler is a METHOD.\n- typescript: `app.get('/a', handler)` -> \"GET /a\", kind=function: the node stands for a registration CALL expression.\n- go: `http.HandleFunc(\"/a\", handler)` in main -> \"ANY /a\", kind=function: also a call.\nTwo axioms bear on it:\n- ADR-0027: \"Symbol.kind names the source-language syntactic construct that the symbol represents.\" Audit-findings 0013's row for `route` says \"Fold: kind=function/method + meta['framework_role']='route'\", so method was anticipated, but the producer emits function for every case.\n- ADR-0031: language \"names the source language in which this Symbol's declaration appears, or None if the Symbol does not represent a declaration\"; protocol_origin names the family a synthetic stand-in stands for. A marker for a registration call is a synthetic stand-in, yet it carries language=java/typescript/go and protocol_origin=None.\nQuestion for the owner: what does a route marker represent? (a) the handler's declaration: then kind should follow the handler (function vs method) and the node is a second node for one declaration; (b) a synthetic route stand-in: then language=None + protocol_origin set, and kind needs a construct that is not 'function'. WI-ziruv records this as a candidate falsification and ships no test for it until it is ruled."  # 43e3
    fields: {}  # 43e3
- op: discuss  # f8c6
  at: '2026-10-27T21:26:30Z'  # f8c6
  by: agent  # f8c6
  actor: jgstern_agent  # f8c6
  clock: 2  # f8c6
  nonce: f8c6  # f8c6
  message: "2026-10-27 INVESTIGATION (owner-requested; ADRs, spec, code, live survey on dev 2fe7978820). Recommendation: option (b). The marker is a synthetic stand-in for the ROUTE, i.e. ADR-0031 Class B. Correction to this item's description: (b) does NOT need a kind other than `function`.\n\nWHY NOT (a), \"the handler's declaration\": the code and the ADRs already rule it out.\n- make_route_symbol (analyze/base.py:1267) names the marker \"{METHOD} {path}\" and says \"The handler's own name is NOT the record name\". It anchors the marker at the REGISTRATION call, and one handler gets several markers at one span (a multi-method registration). The handler is a separate node, reached by a dispatches_to edge from the marker (live: express, spring, go, rails).\n- ADR-0035 types `route` as LOGICAL identity, a thing that exists once whatever code refers to it, beside topics and channels. Its v8 amendment, the owner's 2026-06-16 ruling, calls routing a CBV method through the route factory \"a category error (a method is a file-anchored declaration, not a LOGICAL route)\".\n- Spec §entrypoints already calls a marker \"a route registration\", which \"is not importable API\".\n\nWHY (b): ADR-0031 Class B is \"synthetic stand-ins representing entities with no source-language declaration\". Its own table already put the two route-shaped linkers there: grpc's Route synthetic (language=None, protocol_origin=grpc) and openapi operations (\"spec-derived routes\"). The code-registered markers are the only route family left Class A. make_route_symbol's docstring draws its line at \"fabricated from a protocol definition rather than a real source declaration\", but `app.get('/a', h)` is not a declaration of the route either.\n\nKIND: every Class-B LOGICAL stand-in in the tree is kind=function + meta.framework_role. That covers message_queue, event_sourcing, websocket, ipc, graphql_resolver and openapi; ADR-0027 Phase 3 set it and ADR-0031's Context restates it. So routes keep `function` too, and need no kind of their own. Whether `function` is honest for ANY stand-in is a family-wide question under ADR-0027's axiom. If raised, it belongs to its own item covering all ~20 families, not to this one. The harm a pseudo-function kind did (dead-code flagging \"GET ...\" stand-ins, http.py's call_site docstring) is already closed by INV-disin keying on protocol_origin, which route markers would gain under (b).\n\nFIX SHAPE under (b), a migration rather than a one-liner:\n1. Every make_route_symbol caller and materialize_route_symbols: language=None, discovery_language=host, protocol_origin from the route's transport (http; websocket / grpc / phoenix_ipc for WS / RPC / LIVE). The `http` registry description (\"client calls\") widens to server routes.\n2. Consumers to re-check: widen_route_stable_ids keys route_site:{language}, so stable ids change (an ADR-0035 identity bump); entrypoint ranking's language weight; go and rails put the http_route entrypoint ON the marker, and INV-disin notes language-scoped seeds cannot match a language=None node, so --entry auto and slice need a test; INV-disin's dead-code comment about \"Class-A route callables\"; sketch and routes display. Per-language metrics already fall back to discovery_language (spec, per-language attribution).\n3. A bakeoff, as ADR-0031 Phase 1 had.\nObserved in passing, not filed: the http_route entrypoint sits on the HANDLER for express, spring and flask (flask has no marker at all) but on the MARKER for go and rails. In spring, the class contains a \"GET /a\" function."  # f8c6
- op: discuss  # 1dbd
